@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Replace selfauth's jwx dependency
+
+Selfauth now signs RS256 tokens with the existing `github.com/golang-jwt/jwt/v4`, stores `*rsa.PrivateKey` / `*rsa.PublicKey`, and publishes an explicit RSA JWKS using `encoding/json`. The original fixed key, issuer, audience array, expiry, empty subject, identity claims, access-token hash, random JWT ID, response fields, and headers are preserved. The old token and JWKS have **no `kid`**; its absence is preserved. The original promoted-field RSA literal is retained as required by this repository’s `embedlit` analyzer.
+
+## Premise verification
+
+Before editing, `rg 'lestrrat-go|lestrrat_go|golang-jwt|golang_jwt' --glob '*.go' --glob BUILD --glob go.mod` showed selfauth as the only first-party jwx user and numerous existing golang-jwt/v4 users. Selfauth itself is live (registered by the enterprise server and referenced by OIDC), so its behavior is preserved.
+
+A temporary program outside the repository using jwx v1.2.29 and the original fixed RSA parameters captured its JSON and JWT header/payload before replacement. `testdata/jwks.json` contains the exact old HTTP body, including field order, indentation, unpadded base64url parameters, and lack of a trailing newline. Tests compare the bytes and verify a token using the published modulus/exponent through both golang-jwt and independent `crypto/rsa.VerifyPKCS1v15`, as well as checking all claims and the token endpoint response.
+
+## Measurements
+
+The same `bazel query 'deps(//enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth)'` was run on the original and changed BUILD/source. Counts include source-file and metadata labels, not just compiled libraries. External labels were counted with `rg '^@'`; repositories are unique prefixes before `//`.
+
+| Measure | Before | After | Change |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Transitive dependency labels (`wc -l`) | 4,835 | 4,692 | -143 |
+| External dependency labels (`rg '^@' ... \| wc -l`) | 4,488 | 4,345 | -143 |
+| External repositories (unique label prefixes) | 105 | 99 | -6 |
+| Direct library deps (BUILD dependency strings) | 9 | 7 | -2 |
+| Direct external library deps | 4 | 2 | -2 |
+| Declared Go targets (`rg -c '^go_(library\|test)\(' BUILD`) | 1 | 2 | +1 test |
+| Production source LOC (`wc -l selfauth.go`) | 268 | 257 | -11 |
+
+The after dependency set is a strict subset of the before set: no labels were added. Exactly jwx plus its five lestrrat helpers disappear; golang-jwt/v4 was already present transitively. Tests add 125 Go LOC and a nine-line golden fixture. Module declarations remain unchanged pending the separate dependency-cleanup PR.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `bazel query 'deps(//enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth)'` before and after: passed; counts above.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(//..., //enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth, 1)'`: failed while preloading the unrelated `default_execution_image` repository because its Docker build timed out. No build was stopped merely for being slow. Source/BUILD search identified `//enterprise/server/cmd/server:server_lib` and `//enterprise/server/oidc:oidc` as the direct existing users. The focused query `bazel query 'rdeps(set(//enterprise/server/cmd/server:server_lib //enterprise/server/oidc:oidc //enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth //enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth_test), //enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth, 1)'` passed and returned exactly those four targets (the two users, the changed library, and its new test).
+- `bazel test --jobs=2 --remote_executor= //enterprise/server/selfauth:selfauth_test`: the first invocation executed both tests successfully, but failed build-time `embedlit` validation on an explicit `rsa.PublicKey` literal. The original repository-style literal was restored; the final rerun passed, including both interoperability tests and analyzer validation.
+- `bazel build --jobs=2 --remote_executor= $(cat /tmp/selfauth-rdeps)`: passed for all four targets, including the enterprise server library and OIDC, with analyzer validation enabled (3,303 seconds; 12,514 actions).
+- `go test -mod=readonly ./enterprise/server/selfauth`: unavailable as a standalone Go package because generated protobuf packages are provided by Bazel; failed during package setup.
+- Supplemental `cd /tmp/selfauth-harness && go test -mod=mod -v .`: both tests passed. This temporary harness retained the RSA constructor, signing, JWKS and response code and test source, with registration dependencies removed, issuer/logging stubbed, and an equivalent standard-Go embedded-key initializer; it does not substitute for the Bazel checks.
+- `git diff --check`: passed.
+
+Long Bazel commands were launched under `nohup`, logged in `/tmp/selfauth-query.log`, `/tmp/selfauth-focused-query.log`, `/tmp/selfauth-validation.log`, and `/tmp/selfauth-retest.log`, and polled. No remote execution was enabled. The unrelated failed Docker repository build left 3.527 GB of inactive build cache; `docker builder prune -f` reclaimed it to keep local validation supplied with disk space. Later, about 1.9 GB of completed Bazel download archives older than ten minutes were removed from the download cache, retaining extracted repositories and build outputs.
+
+## Dependency cleanup and scope
+
+After the change, `rg 'github.com/(lestrrat-go|goccy/go-json)|com_github_(lestrrat_go|goccy_go_json)' --glob '*.go' --glob BUILD --glob BUILD.bazel .` returns no matches. `github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx` now has no first-party source or BUILD users. The same is true of its helper-module candidates `github.com/lestrrat-go/backoff/v2`, `github.com/lestrrat-go/blackmagic`, `github.com/lestrrat-go/httpcc`, `github.com/lestrrat-go/iter`, `github.com/lestrrat-go/option`, and `github.com/goccy/go-json`. The baseline Bazel graph includes jwx and the five lestrrat helpers, but not goccy/go-json; do not interpret the estimated six indirect modules as six additional Bazel repositories eliminated. Full Go module pruning is left to the serialized dependency-cleanup PR.
+
+No shared dependency files were edited, no binary-size reduction is claimed, and no constructor/API cleanup was attempted. All implementation, BUILD, fixture, and test changes are within `enterprise/server/selfauth/`. The only file outside that scope is this explicitly requested root-level `result.md` deliverable. No push or PR was performed.
